# Pin the PUBLIC registry for this repo, so `resolved` URLs in package-lock.json
# can never record a private mirror from whatever machine ran `npm install`.
#
# If your default registry is an internal mirror and npmjs is unreachable, this
# will make `npm install` fail rather than silently bake the mirror's hostname
# into a public lockfile. That is the intended behaviour. To install anyway:
#   npm install --registry=<your-mirror> && bash scripts/check-leaks.sh --fix
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
